        "scanners": {
          "vt": {
            "status": "suspicious",
            "verdict": "suspicious",
            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "analysis": "Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: team-dispatch\nVersion: 1.0.5\n\nThe bundle implements a complex multi-agent orchestration system that performs extensive system-level modifications and establishes persistence. Key indicators include `scripts/setup.sh`, which modifies the core `openclaw.json` configuration to grant broad `subagents.allowAgents` permissions, and `scripts/watch-install.sh`, which installs persistent background services via `launchd`, `systemd`, or `cron` to run a monitoring script (`scripts/watch.py`). While these high-risk behaviors are documented and aligned with the stated purpose of managing task dependencies (DAG), the combination of persistence and system-wide configuration changes represents a significant attack surface without clear evidence of malicious intent.",
            "source": "palm",
            "checkedAt": 1773002525353
          },
          "skillspector": null,
          "llm": {
            "status": "suspicious",
            "verdict": "suspicious",
            "normalizedStatus": "suspicious",
            "confidence": "medium",
            "summary": "The skill's files and instructions match a multi-agent dispatcher, but its install/run instructions modify global OpenClaw agent configuration, install persistent watchers, and enable broad subagent permissions—actions that are coherent with the advertised purpose but carry notable security/scope risks and should be reviewed before running.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "The skill's name/description (multi‑agent orchestration) aligns with the included assets: agent templates, DAG/project templates, watcher scripts, and setup scripts that create agent workspaces and dispatching behavior. However, the setup explicitly writes into global OpenClaw config (openclaw.json) and configures a 'main' dispatcher with subagents.allowAgents: [\"*\"], which is broader than a minimal skill install—plausibly intended but worth confirmation.",
                "label": "Purpose & Capability",
                "name": "purpose_capability",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
                "detail": "SKILL.md instructs running scripts/setup.sh that will create symlinks, write ~/.openclaw/configs/team-dispatch.json, copy assets into ~/.openclaw/agents/<id>, create workspace/sessions, modify openclaw.json entries (adding main + subagents), and restart the Gateway. Those instructions require modifying system/global agent state and creating background jobs; they go beyond a purely local helper and grant the dispatcher broad control over agent configuration.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
                "name": "instruction_scope",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "There is no external install spec (instruction-only), but the package includes many shell/Python scripts (setup.sh, watch.sh, watch.py, launchd plist, Windows scheduled task installer). Scripts are bundled (no obvious external download URLs in provided files), which reduces supply-chain unknowns, but executing them will write files, create scheduled tasks/launchd plists, and restart services—operations that deserve manual review.",
                "label": "Install Mechanism",
                "name": "install_mechanism",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The skill declares no required environment variables or primary credential. Optional notification features (Telegram chatId) and model names are present in configs but disabled by default. Requesting no external secrets is proportionate to the stated purpose; still, if you enable notifications or model access, you will need to provide credentials externally.",
                "label": "Credentials",
                "name": "environment_proportionality",
                "rating": "ok"
